nthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:31:26Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…zz 92aeb09eace0008b)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_regexp` arm flagged a \\\"match\\nmeter\\\" divergence on a 3-byte input (sha256 663a47b2…21adb2) that folds,\\nthrough `gen_regexp`, into a deeply nested backreference-heavy,\\nempty-matchable pattern (dotall `s`) over the subject \\\"a\\\"@0. Matching it\\ndispatches 470334 metered steps, so the raw 16.16 match meter is\\n470334*65536 = 30_823_809_024 — past 2^32.\\n\\nBoth engines dispatch the identical step histogram; the port's meter was\\nnever wrong. XS's `meterIndex` is a txU8 and the port meters into a u64,\\nholding the full value. The oracle shim's now-fixed 32-bit copy wrapped it\\nto 30_823_809_024 mod 2^32 = 759_037_952, a phantom divergence against the\\nport's correct figure — the same harness-side truncation as sibling\\nfinding 5d122a6fc10babd9, whose fix (widening the oracle's meter fields to\\n64 bit) already subsumes this input. Verified: reproduces at the fuzzed SHA\\n38ca1d18 (divergence \\\"match meter ironhorse=30823809024 pin=759037952\\\");\\nclean at the standing-branch HEAD, which carries the widening fix.\\n\\nRegression: ironhorse-vm `finding_92aeb09eace0008b_regexp_meter_overflow`\\nreplays the exact case through the port's `compile`+`match_regexp`,\\nasserting no panic and the full-width meter (30_823_809_024 > u32::MAX,\\nnever the 759_037_952 wrap). Builds without the oracle or the c/moddable\\nsubmodule, per the standing-branch convention.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp match-meter overflow (fu…\",\"oid\":\"938ff59f18e27c6628c4deea3d714de2f9f425c8\"}],\"headRefName\":\"ironhorse-fuzz-findings\",\"headRepositoryOwner\":{\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\"},\"isDraft\":fa